    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0414" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg294"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Lorillard to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-12-19"><hi rendition="#italic">December 19,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that a general
                    treaty of arbitration between Denmark and Italy was signed on the 14th instant
                    at Rome.</p>
                <p>While the text of the treaty has not yet been made public, I am in a position to
                    state that by its terms all differences which may occur between the two
                    countries are to be referred to the Permanent Court of. Arbitration at The Hague
                    for final settlement.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George L.
                    Lorillard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
